# Language conventions

## Chat
- Always communicate with the user in **Spanish**.

## Project code and assets
- All **UI text**, **file names**, **folder names**, **CSS class names**, **IDs**, **comments**, and **commit messages** must be in **English**.
- Do not invent Spanish identifiers or comments in source files.

### Examples

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<a href="#inicio">Inicio</a>
<p class="hero__rol">desarrollador de software</p>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<a href="#home">Home</a>
<p class="hero__role">software developer</p>
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
/* Estilos del menú flotante */

/* ✅ GOOD */
/* Floating menu styles */
```

```text
❌ BAD file: estilos/estilo.css
✅ GOOD file: styles/style.css
```

When renaming existing Spanish labels for this rule, update HTML, CSS selectors, and any JS references together.
